1
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:47,440
Hello, Mom. I'll call you back.
I'm busy right now.

2
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:49,720
<i>Do you have Louis? Did you hear me?</i>

3
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:53,920
I knew it. I knew I couldn't trust you.

4
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,080
Don't!

5
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:57,280
Out of bullets, huh?

6
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:01,120
<i>You guys are still alive?</i>

7
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:03,600
Looks like you're close to Aek, huh?

8
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:06,160
Are you his daughter?

9
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:09,480
Stop talking and tell me where he is!

10
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:13,040
-Don't!
-Hey!

11
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,240
Don't move.

12
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:17,800
If you hadn't interfered,
I would've found out where my dad is.

13
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:20,040
You don't understand anything, do you?

14
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:29,680
Risa.

15
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:33,760
Risa, calm down. Risa.

16
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:41,040
Hey, Mungkorn.

17
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,680
Mungkorn, where are you going?

18
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:58,720
<i>You trust Koh more than you trust me now?</i>

19
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:02,240
I asked him for help
because he knew my dad,

20
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:05,240
and he promised to help me find him.

21
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:06,520
<i>That's all.</i>

22
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,760
Then why can't you tell me
what you're really planning?

23
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:11,160
I don't want anyone else
risking their life because of me anymore.

24
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,560
Then why is Koh allowed to?

25
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:15,160
Do you see me as an outsider now?

26
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:25,480
This is all because of you.

27
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:30,080
If you hadn't interfered,
I would've found out where my dad is.

28
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:41,480
Because of you. If you hadn't interfered,

29
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:43,920
I would've found out where my dad is.

30
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,400
You really don't understand anything.

31
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:49,080
Why did you get involved?

32
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:51,560
You really don't understand anything.

33
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:53,080
Isn't it your fault?

34
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,360
You don't understand anything.

35
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:58,520
<i>Why did you get involved?</i>

36
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:04,280
<i>Why? Isn't it your fault?</i>

37
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:09,560
<i>Why did you get involved?</i>

38
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:12,760
Why did you get involved?

39
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,880
Because I love you!

40
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:24,680
Thanks.

41
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:33,120
Still thinking about Louis?

42
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:41,200
We still have a chance to go after him.
Don't worry.

43
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:46,920
Was I too harsh

44
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:50,080
on Mungkorn last night?

45
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:57,000
To be fair,

46
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:59,080
he wasn't really wrong.

47
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:02,320
I was just still angry at him.

48
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:09,720
Have you talked to him yet?

49
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:20,760
Don't overthink it.
If you're in the wrong, just apologize.

50
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:25,240
If only it were that easy.

51
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,880
What's so hard about it?

52
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:35,800
Well, ever since I've known him,

53
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:39,440
I've never seen him this angry before.

54
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:06,440
RISA

55
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,600
Who are you here to see?

56
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:29,120
What's all that noise?

57
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:31,760
Sorry, the coffee will have to wait.

58
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:35,400
It's all spilled.

59
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:44,240
Surprised I'm still alive, sir?

60
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,800
You were lucky to survive.

61
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:57,520
But I'm surprised
you came here looking for death.

62
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,360
I'm like a cornered dog.

63
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:07,320
But a cornered dog
is willing to risk everything.

64
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:16,320
That only works
when both sides are of equal value.

65
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:17,840
You know that, right?

66
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,960
My life

67
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,880
for yours.

68
00:09:26,280 --> 00:09:27,680
Is that a fair trade?

69
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:44,280
You think your life is worth that much?

70
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:52,120
If you were planning to betray me,
you should've come better prepared.

71
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,880
What are you talking about?

72
00:09:57,800 --> 00:10:00,080
You're the one who betrayed me.

73
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:02,320
When did I betray you?

74
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:04,920
You hired that Admin gang

75
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,480
to stab me in the back, didn't you?

76
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:11,960
But you said you killed them all.

77
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:16,040
Hey.

78
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:18,840
What the hell are you talking about?

79
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:23,840
Don't tell me you don't know about this.

80
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:49,680
I get it now. This must've been

81
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:52,520
the Admin gang's plan all along.

82
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:55,120
They're trying to turn us
against each other.

83
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:59,280
What are you talking about?
I don't understand.

84
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,920
RISA

85
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:30,000
I was double-crossed.
They made me believe they were dead.

86
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:33,320
They infiltrated the waste facility

87
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:36,040
and came up with a plan
to steal the money truck.

88
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:39,960
They staged it to look like an accident.

89
00:11:42,320 --> 00:11:45,880
Their plan was to expose
my online gambling operation

90
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:50,960
and your waste facility
that was being used for money laundering,

91
00:11:51,040 --> 00:11:54,760
so we'd stop trusting each other,
and they succeeded.

92
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:00,880
Sir.

93
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:04,600
I think we should go back
to the way things were

94
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:08,400
and work together
to hunt those bastards down.

95
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:14,040
How can I trust
that you're telling the truth?

96
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,280
I've worked for you for a long time.

97
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,480
I think you know what kind of person I am.

98
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,200
Here.

99
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:42,600
If you don't trust me,
have your men verify it.

100
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:45,160
See for yourself
whether I'm involved in this or not.

101
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:51,320
It contains information
on every member of the Admin gang.

102
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,360
KONGKIAT KAMNERDRAT

103
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:03,760
CIVIL REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE

104
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:10,240
SORAWIT SAKUNTHON

105
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:17,800
Are you absolutely sure

106
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:20,280
these are all the Admin gang members?

107
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:23,360
Yes, sir.

108
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:32,200
I see. We'll deal with them first.

109
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:35,120
Then we'll settle things between us.

110
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:42,240
I'll be waiting for your good news, sir.

111
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:56,200
CIVIL REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE

112
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:10,360
You don't need to see me off.

113
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:54,680
MEET AT THE BASE IN TWO HOURS

114
00:14:58,280 --> 00:14:59,680
Admin is calling everyone.

115
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
I got the message.

116
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:05,720
Have you talked things through
with Mungkorn?

117
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:12,760
I tried calling him, but he didn't answer.
I guess he's still mad.

118
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:18,600
You can make up with him when you see him.
For now, pack your things.

119
00:15:18,680 --> 00:15:20,160
Chen's coming to pick us up.

120
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:42,720
-Coffee. Drink, drank, drunk.
-Yes.

121
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:48,280
Ris.

122
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:54,480
Hey, why are you riding with Koh?

123
00:15:56,840 --> 00:16:00,400
You're late. What were you two doing?

124
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:02,600
-Oh, interesting.
-Wow.

125
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:07,400
Hey, Yak. Are those two doing that?

126
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:17,400
Wait, bro. What exactly
do you mean by "doing that"?

127
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:21,160
You don't know?
It's some kind of rhythmic activity.

128
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:24,920
Hey, cut it out.

129
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,160
We're here to work, not fool around.

130
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:28,040
Why so serious?

131
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:31,640
Hey, Ris. Didn't Mung come with you?

132
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:33,680
No.

133
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:36,320
Let's get started.

134
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:39,880
Hold on. Aren't we waiting for Mungkorn?

135
00:16:41,480 --> 00:16:43,520
We don't have time to wait for anyone.

136
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:47,000
The next mission starts tonight.

137
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:49,040
What? Tonight?

138
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:52,640
We don't even have time to prepare.

139
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:54,600
Admin has already prepared everything.

140
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:02,320
<i>Hello, everyone.</i>

141
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:05,440
<i>Congratulations on the success</i>
<i>of the last mission.</i>

142
00:17:05,520 --> 00:17:07,560
<i>Everything went according to plan.</i>

143
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:11,640
<i>What you're about to hear</i>

144
00:17:12,320 --> 00:17:15,280
<i>is our final mission.</i>

145
00:17:22,119 --> 00:17:26,760
<i>Thanks to your work</i>
<i>driving a wedge between Wisut and Louis,</i>

146
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:31,240
<i>Wisut's money-laundering operation</i>
<i>has been disrupted.</i>

147
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:34,639
<i>The waste facility is no longer secure.</i>

148
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:37,879
<i>Until a new cash storage system is ready,</i>

149
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:42,320
<i>they've been forced</i>
<i>to move 800 million baht in dirty money</i>

150
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:45,320
<i>into Wisut's own house.</i>

151
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:22,160
All done.

152
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:46,360
MUNGKORN, WHERE ARE YOU?
I WANT TO TALK AND CLEAR THINGS UP

153
00:18:58,640 --> 00:18:59,960
Ready to go?

154
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:08,800
Want some?

155
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:11,440
I'm good.

156
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:20,360
Snacks help you relax, you know.

157
00:19:21,840 --> 00:19:23,000
Angpao.

158
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:27,880
I need to tell you something.

159
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:34,160
Finally. I've been waiting forever.

160
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:37,720
Go on.

161
00:19:43,400 --> 00:19:45,280
Koh and I

162
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:50,120
tried to capture Louis, but he got away.

163
00:19:54,840 --> 00:19:55,920
If I were you,

164
00:19:58,240 --> 00:19:59,760
I probably would've done the same thing.

165
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:08,000
So, any new leads on your dad?

166
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:17,920
I'm sorry.

167
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:24,920
I went off-plan again.

168
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:29,640
Honestly,

169
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:34,440
Hong and the others expected

170
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:38,520
you'd do something like this
sooner or later.

171
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,520
They won't be mad at you.

172
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:46,240
Really.

173
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:53,600
Does Mung know about this?

174
00:20:58,480 --> 00:21:00,440
-He secretly followed me.
-What?

175
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:07,240
When he found out, he was furious.

176
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:12,000
He said I was putting
everyone else in danger.

177
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:18,800
Don't tell me

178
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:22,520
that's why he didn't show up today.

179
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:24,960
I don't know.

180
00:21:27,520 --> 00:21:30,760
I've called him so many times,
but he won't answer.

181
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:35,600
I think he's upset

182
00:21:37,320 --> 00:21:39,440
because you didn't tell him.

183
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:48,080
Ris.

184
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:51,240
Back in Poipet, he really cared about you.

185
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:56,760
Even after he got shot, the first person
he asked about when he woke up was you.

186
00:21:57,280 --> 00:21:58,560
Don't you see?

187
00:21:58,640 --> 00:22:02,760
All that annoying, overprotective
behavior, it's because of that.

188
00:22:09,640 --> 00:22:12,480
You know, don't you? Mung likes you.

189
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:32,320
We've set up checkpoints
covering every possible escape route.

190
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:33,880
But so far,

191
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:37,200
there's still no sign of Louis.

192
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:42,760
He has to come out eventually.
He can't stay hidden forever.

193
00:22:43,600 --> 00:22:45,680
-Find him and bring him in.
-Yes, sir.

194
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:53,200
POL.LT.GEN. THAMMARONG INTHARASA

195
00:22:56,720 --> 00:22:59,960
Excuse me, sir. A package has arrived.
It's addressed to you.

196
00:23:01,640 --> 00:23:02,680
POL.LT.GEN. THAMMARONG INTHARASA

197
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:40,320
<i>Hello, General.</i>

198
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:46,120
So you're Admin.

199
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:50,160
<i>I'm glad we finally get to speak.</i>

200
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:53,320
What do you want?

201
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:59,560
<i>I have an offer for you.</i>

202
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:14,400
Hey, idiot. What did you do
to make Dad this angry?

203
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:24,960
I'm talking to you. Answer me.

204
00:24:26,760 --> 00:24:31,080
If you want to know that badly,
go ask Dad yourself.

205
00:24:41,640 --> 00:24:43,200
Listen, you jinx.

206
00:24:43,280 --> 00:24:46,440
I won't let you hurt my family.

207
00:24:49,680 --> 00:24:51,200
What the hell are you laughing at?

208
00:24:52,520 --> 00:24:53,960
At someone who claims to love his family.

209
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:57,960
You keep wasting Dad's money

210
00:24:58,040 --> 00:24:59,840
on failed business ideas.

211
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:05,040
You're always getting into trouble,
and Dad has to clean up your mess.

212
00:25:06,040 --> 00:25:09,240
Is that what you call loving your family?

213
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:13,640
-You!
-Enough.

214
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:20,960
Dad, I told you already.

215
00:25:21,040 --> 00:25:23,240
His jinx doesn't belong in our house.

216
00:25:23,320 --> 00:25:25,440
Just tell me what he did.

217
00:25:25,520 --> 00:25:26,960
I'll deal with him myself.

218
00:25:27,040 --> 00:25:29,880
This is none of your concern. Get out.

219
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:40,920
Close the door.

220
00:25:45,360 --> 00:25:49,320
Tell me. Who is this Admin?

221
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:52,760
I don't know.

222
00:25:53,880 --> 00:25:57,840
I only followed his orders.
I've never even seen his face.

223
00:25:57,920 --> 00:25:59,160
Do you realize

224
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:02,400
you've been brainwashed by that Admin?

225
00:26:04,280 --> 00:26:07,640
Don't you see that what you've done

226
00:26:07,720 --> 00:26:11,080
has hurt both yourself and your family?

227
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:16,520
Dad.

228
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:20,200
Stop using family as an excuse.

229
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:26,720
Don't you see
what you're doing is hurting society

230
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:28,520
and other people's families?

231
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:32,480
Everything I did

232
00:26:34,120 --> 00:26:35,840
was so you could have a better life.

233
00:26:38,560 --> 00:26:39,960
Admit it.

234
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:43,760
You did it all for yourself.

235
00:26:51,800 --> 00:26:54,280
Think carefully
about everything you've done.

236
00:26:55,920 --> 00:26:57,520
I'll give you time to decide.

237
00:27:08,440 --> 00:27:09,640
Keep watch.

238
00:27:10,760 --> 00:27:14,960
If my son escapes, you're dead.

239
00:27:15,040 --> 00:27:16,240
Yes, sir.

240
00:27:52,240 --> 00:27:56,160
This evening, Wisut and his family
will attend a high-profile wedding

241
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:58,960
in another province.
From the moment he leaves the house,

242
00:27:59,040 --> 00:28:00,920
you'll have about five hours

243
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:03,720
to break through the security system,

244
00:28:04,560 --> 00:28:07,960
then find the safe and get the money out.

245
00:28:08,040 --> 00:28:10,840
Then stage it to look like a burglary

246
00:28:10,920 --> 00:28:13,880
and call the police to search the house.

247
00:28:16,600 --> 00:28:20,160
I don't think I can hack the CCTV
and security system

248
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:21,600
from outside.

249
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:24,600
The house uses
a satellite internet connection.

250
00:28:26,080 --> 00:28:26,960
You know what I mean?

251
00:28:27,040 --> 00:28:28,520
Hey, I get it.

252
00:28:28,600 --> 00:28:32,680
But does that mean
we have to hack a satellite at NASA?

253
00:28:33,840 --> 00:28:36,400
Why don't we just go
to a planetarium instead, kid?

254
00:28:38,560 --> 00:28:42,480
That's not what I mean. I'm saying
we need to get inside the house first,

255
00:28:42,560 --> 00:28:44,240
then hack the system from there.

256
00:28:44,320 --> 00:28:45,880
What are you talking about, Uncle?

257
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:48,720
Basically, we just need
to get into the house.

258
00:28:48,800 --> 00:28:50,680
Right? That's easy.

259
00:28:50,760 --> 00:28:53,480
Leave it to us. No problem.

260
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:56,040
Whoa, sis. It's not that easy.

261
00:28:56,120 --> 00:28:58,800
A house that big
has to be crawling with guards.

262
00:28:58,880 --> 00:29:01,360
Whatever.

263
00:29:01,440 --> 00:29:03,480
Once we're inside, then what?

264
00:29:04,080 --> 00:29:07,960
Once the security system is down, we'll
deal with the few guards that are left.

265
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:12,960
Louis already took care of most
of the regular staff last time.

266
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:16,200
Compared to our previous jobs,

267
00:29:17,280 --> 00:29:20,800
this one isn't beyond
your abilities, right?

268
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:22,960
It's as easy as peeling a banana.

269
00:29:23,560 --> 00:29:25,920
This is nothing for us.

270
00:29:27,600 --> 00:29:29,560
-I agree, man.
-Yeah.

271
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:36,920
Alright, everyone.
Good luck on your final mission.

272
00:29:40,960 --> 00:29:43,120
-Go!
-Let's go, you guys.

273
00:29:43,200 --> 00:29:44,880
Go!

274
00:29:44,960 --> 00:29:46,320
-Let's move.
-Let's go, bro.

275
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:54,240
Don't lose focus. Let's finish this first.

276
00:29:54,320 --> 00:29:55,880
We can deal with Mungkorn afterward.

277
00:30:06,920 --> 00:30:08,920
The car is ready, sir. This way.

278
00:30:59,240 --> 00:31:00,400
Ugh!

279
00:31:00,480 --> 00:31:02,120
Why are you so pumped?

280
00:31:03,720 --> 00:31:04,720
Turn it off.

281
00:31:26,440 --> 00:31:29,720
<i>Risa, you ready? I'm starting now.</i>

282
00:31:33,440 --> 00:31:35,800
We're ready. Go ahead, sis.

283
00:31:44,760 --> 00:31:45,720
Yes, Ms. Moei.

284
00:31:47,040 --> 00:31:48,320
This is Chin.

285
00:31:49,440 --> 00:31:51,760
Go check Mungkorn's room for my phone.

286
00:31:51,840 --> 00:31:53,200
If you find it, call me.

287
00:31:53,960 --> 00:31:56,000
-Yes, sir.
<i>-Be careful.</i>

288
00:31:56,080 --> 00:31:59,200
If he gets out, you know what'll happen.

289
00:32:00,120 --> 00:32:01,200
Yes, sir.

290
00:32:06,360 --> 00:32:10,080
Mr. Mungkorn, may I come in?

291
00:32:15,200 --> 00:32:17,960
Mr. Mungkorn? Mr. Mungkorn!

292
00:32:27,880 --> 00:32:29,200
The bars are still intact.

293
00:32:30,960 --> 00:32:32,400
How the hell did he get out?

294
00:32:34,280 --> 00:32:36,560
-Mr. Mungkorn!
-Looking for this?

295
00:32:39,840 --> 00:32:43,360
Or maybe this?
Do you know what halothane is?

296
00:32:44,200 --> 00:32:45,200
What?

297
00:32:45,800 --> 00:32:47,880
A volatile anesthetic gas.

298
00:32:50,560 --> 00:32:51,440
Mr. Mungkorn!

299
00:32:53,240 --> 00:32:54,560
Mr. Mungkorn!

300
00:32:55,240 --> 00:32:56,440
Open the door, Mr. Mungkorn!

301
00:33:12,880 --> 00:33:15,520
Help! Somebody help me!

302
00:33:15,600 --> 00:33:17,320
-What was that?
-Let's check it out.

303
00:33:18,880 --> 00:33:21,920
Help me! Somebody help!

304
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,400
Stop screaming! Quiet!

305
00:33:23,480 --> 00:33:25,400
-Got any money? Hand it over, pretty lady.
-Hey!

306
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:26,680
Stop right there!

307
00:33:26,760 --> 00:33:28,240
Hey! Run!

308
00:33:28,320 --> 00:33:29,680
-Go!
-Give it back!

309
00:33:29,760 --> 00:33:30,960
-Give me back my bag!
-Stop!

310
00:33:31,040 --> 00:33:32,920
They stole my bag!

311
00:33:35,840 --> 00:33:38,480
Angpao. Angpao, come here.

312
00:33:39,320 --> 00:33:40,960
Hurry.

313
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:44,800
Let's go.

314
00:33:49,920 --> 00:33:51,920
Over there. Go.

315
00:33:54,960 --> 00:33:56,000
Hurry.

316
00:34:35,640 --> 00:34:37,479
Go. Run.

317
00:34:39,360 --> 00:34:40,600
Hey! Stop right there!

318
00:34:46,519 --> 00:34:47,560
Where did he go?

319
00:34:49,959 --> 00:34:51,560
We were just running together.

320
00:35:13,560 --> 00:35:15,000
The security system is down.

321
00:35:15,080 --> 00:35:18,320
Okay. We're ready. Move in.

322
00:35:35,440 --> 00:35:36,720
Chen.

323
00:35:37,240 --> 00:35:38,440
Yeah. Be careful.

324
00:35:45,240 --> 00:35:46,640
Ugh, why isn't it working?

325
00:35:47,560 --> 00:35:48,920
Come on.

326
00:35:58,640 --> 00:36:01,600
There are two guards at the front gate
and two at the back.

327
00:36:01,680 --> 00:36:03,040
Be careful.

328
00:36:23,560 --> 00:36:24,800
You sure you won't miss?

329
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:27,000
Wanna find out?

330
00:36:48,520 --> 00:36:49,840
Let's move.

331
00:37:15,960 --> 00:37:17,000
Come on.

332
00:37:22,960 --> 00:37:24,760
-Sis.
-Hey, you scared me!

333
00:37:24,840 --> 00:37:26,320
It's me. What's wrong?

334
00:37:26,400 --> 00:37:28,480
I don't know what's wrong with this gun.
It won't fire.

335
00:37:28,560 --> 00:37:33,720
See? That's why I hate using guns.

336
00:37:33,800 --> 00:37:36,600
Sis, don't worry. I'll handle it.

337
00:37:36,680 --> 00:37:38,640
-Are you crazy?
-What?

338
00:37:38,720 --> 00:37:40,960
You're going in empty-handed?
You'll get yourself killed.

339
00:37:42,320 --> 00:37:45,360
Killed? Come on.
Let me tell you something.

340
00:37:45,440 --> 00:37:48,200
Guns are far more dangerous.
They're a much bigger risk.

341
00:37:48,280 --> 00:37:51,720
<i>Even a tranquilizer gun can kill</i>
<i>or cripple you if it hits the wrong spot.</i>

342
00:37:51,800 --> 00:37:54,840
We're here to rob a house,
not run a charity.

343
00:37:54,920 --> 00:37:56,360
Stop trying to be a saint.

344
00:37:57,720 --> 00:38:00,680
Hey, why are the two guards
at the back acting weird?

345
00:38:01,440 --> 00:38:02,560
-Sis.
-What?

346
00:38:02,640 --> 00:38:05,000
-What are you talking about?
-Where did they go?

347
00:38:08,120 --> 00:38:09,120
What are you doing here?

348
00:38:11,200 --> 00:38:13,480
-We're here for charity.
-Charity my ass.

349
00:38:14,720 --> 00:38:16,880
Hey, call the boss.

350
00:38:21,160 --> 00:38:22,280
Hey, hold on!

351
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:41,120
You two!

352
00:38:43,800 --> 00:38:47,120
Grab their weapons and follow me.

353
00:38:48,280 --> 00:38:50,560
Okay. Let's go.

354
00:38:50,640 --> 00:38:55,200
He's fine. The dart hit his chest muscle.
What about this guy?

355
00:38:56,720 --> 00:38:58,920
-He's okay. No major arteries hit. Go.
-Go.

356
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:01,760
Those two old guys have pretty good aim.

357
00:39:23,080 --> 00:39:24,240
The hallway's clear.

358
00:39:33,840 --> 00:39:34,840
Go.

359
00:40:03,400 --> 00:40:04,760
We're even now, okay?

360
00:40:17,520 --> 00:40:19,320
Dining room's clear.

361
00:40:26,760 --> 00:40:31,000
Clear. No one's left.
Just find the safe and get the money out.

362
00:40:32,760 --> 00:40:34,800
Yeah. This is way too easy.

363
00:40:38,880 --> 00:40:41,120
What was that? Is someone else still here?

364
00:40:43,320 --> 00:40:45,240
Everyone, be careful.

365
00:40:45,320 --> 00:40:48,040
<i>There's still someone on the second floor.</i>

366
00:40:48,640 --> 00:40:50,280
Where are they, Angpao?

367
00:40:50,360 --> 00:40:53,080
No idea. I caught a glimpse of them
just now, then they disappeared.

368
00:40:53,160 --> 00:40:55,360
Then find them.

369
00:41:14,120 --> 00:41:15,680
What the hell is this?

370
00:41:38,840 --> 00:41:41,320
Everyone, I think something's off.

371
00:41:43,680 --> 00:41:44,600
Any sign of him?

372
00:41:46,400 --> 00:41:49,040
Look carefully.
Is it a ghost or something?

373
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:52,800
Huh? Seriously?

374
00:41:53,760 --> 00:41:57,680
Ghost or not, I don't care. I'll knock
it out with my tranquilizer gun.

375
00:41:58,760 --> 00:42:01,120
-Why don't you just shoot it?
-Oh, I will.

376
00:42:03,640 --> 00:42:06,760
Let's split up. You guys search upstairs.

377
00:42:06,840 --> 00:42:08,840
Risa and I will search downstairs. Okay?

378
00:42:08,920 --> 00:42:11,800
Hold on. When you say "split up,"

379
00:42:11,880 --> 00:42:14,360
do you mean to find the safe or the ghost?

380
00:42:14,440 --> 00:42:18,320
Both, obviously.

381
00:42:18,400 --> 00:42:22,960
Alright. You take the front stairs.
Yak and I will take the back.

382
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:24,000
-Got it.
-Okay.

383
00:42:24,080 --> 00:42:26,560
If anyone finds anything, report it.
Let's finish this.

384
00:42:26,640 --> 00:42:28,000
-Got it.
-Move.

385
00:43:27,200 --> 00:43:28,040
What are you looking at?

386
00:43:42,360 --> 00:43:46,600
Do you think what we're doing is right?

387
00:43:49,160 --> 00:43:50,080
What do you mean?

388
00:43:52,160 --> 00:43:54,040
I know Wisut is a bad person,

389
00:43:54,840 --> 00:43:58,720
but the rest of his family
has nothing to do with this.

390
00:44:00,960 --> 00:44:03,040
If we don't stop Wisut,

391
00:44:03,560 --> 00:44:06,080
even more families
will suffer because of him.

392
00:44:12,240 --> 00:44:13,480
Let's keep looking.

393
00:44:21,640 --> 00:44:25,280
-Come on, sis. Raedy?
-Yeah.

394
00:44:25,360 --> 00:44:26,400
Go.

395
00:44:30,480 --> 00:44:31,840
Hey, bro!

396
00:44:33,400 --> 00:44:34,920
Hey, what are you two doing?

397
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:38,040
We came looking for a ghost,

398
00:44:38,120 --> 00:44:40,200
but instead, we found diamonds.

399
00:44:41,800 --> 00:44:45,440
Whoa. You were just lecturing me
about getting the job done,

400
00:44:45,520 --> 00:44:47,160
and now you're acting like thieves?

401
00:44:47,240 --> 00:44:50,200
What did I do wrong?
I'm just following Admin's orders.

402
00:44:50,280 --> 00:44:52,800
He said to make it look convincing,

403
00:44:52,880 --> 00:44:55,400
so I'm making it look like a real robbery.

404
00:44:55,480 --> 00:44:56,520
Hey.

405
00:44:57,840 --> 00:44:59,440
You're only taking men's stuff.

406
00:44:59,960 --> 00:45:01,480
Huh?

407
00:45:01,560 --> 00:45:03,440
Why don't you grab something
for the ladies too?

408
00:45:03,520 --> 00:45:06,000
I got you something too.

409
00:45:06,080 --> 00:45:07,520
-Look, Hong.
-Look.

410
00:45:07,600 --> 00:45:09,320
-These earrings.
-Nice.

411
00:45:09,400 --> 00:45:11,400
-They're so cute.
-Here, a watch.

412
00:45:15,680 --> 00:45:17,080
A watch…

413
00:45:21,120 --> 00:45:22,280
What?

414
00:45:23,320 --> 00:45:24,160
I just saw someone

415
00:45:24,240 --> 00:45:27,280
at the door. As soon as they saw me,

416
00:45:27,360 --> 00:45:29,080
they slammed the door and ran.

417
00:45:30,400 --> 00:45:32,400
Ghosts don't close doors.

418
00:45:36,880 --> 00:45:37,960
Be careful, bro.

419
00:45:52,480 --> 00:45:54,560
No! Don't shoot!

420
00:45:58,840 --> 00:46:02,360
Angpao? What are you doing up here?

421
00:46:02,440 --> 00:46:06,200
Everything downstairs is done. I didn't
want to stay down there by myself.

422
00:46:06,280 --> 00:46:09,560
Oh, really? So you got scared
of the ghost and ran upstairs?

423
00:46:09,640 --> 00:46:12,800
You already knew? Then why bring up
the ghost in the first place?

424
00:46:15,200 --> 00:46:16,400
I suddenly feel so sleepy.

425
00:46:16,480 --> 00:46:19,000
Huh? Look at you.

426
00:46:19,080 --> 00:46:21,520
Look at you.

427
00:46:21,600 --> 00:46:23,040
What?

428
00:46:23,120 --> 00:46:24,080
-Angpao!
-What the heck?

429
00:46:24,160 --> 00:46:26,080
Wait, why did he fall asleep?

430
00:46:26,160 --> 00:46:29,080
-You missed. You hit here.
-Yeah.

431
00:46:29,160 --> 00:46:30,760
What?

432
00:46:32,760 --> 00:46:33,800
Who says I missed?

433
00:46:36,320 --> 00:46:39,640
-Oh, that's Yak's dart.
-It hit his leg.

434
00:47:39,120 --> 00:47:40,160
I found it.

435
00:47:49,120 --> 00:47:50,040
Be careful.

436
00:47:50,120 --> 00:47:51,560
It's a long dart.

437
00:47:51,640 --> 00:47:54,720
Angpao! What do we do?

438
00:47:54,800 --> 00:47:57,400
-He won't wake up, no matter what. Angpao!
-Huh?

439
00:47:57,480 --> 00:48:00,240
We found the safe.
It's in the room with the pool table.

440
00:48:01,440 --> 00:48:03,160
Let's go, Gao. Show them what you've got.

441
00:48:03,240 --> 00:48:05,080
-It's showtime.
-Yeah.

442
00:48:05,160 --> 00:48:07,120
Wait. Everyone, come back.

443
00:48:07,200 --> 00:48:09,600
What about Angpao?
Are we just going to leave him here?

444
00:48:09,680 --> 00:48:13,360
No, we can't leave him like this.
Take him to the car.

445
00:48:13,440 --> 00:48:16,520
-Okay? Let's go.
-Hold on.

446
00:48:16,600 --> 00:48:20,440
He's not exactly small.
I can't carry him by myself. I need help.

447
00:48:24,280 --> 00:48:25,160
Yeah.

448
00:48:25,240 --> 00:48:27,160
You don't know
how to crack the safe anyway.

449
00:48:34,160 --> 00:48:36,480
Wisut's dirty money must be inside.

450
00:48:36,560 --> 00:48:37,680
You got this?

451
00:48:39,600 --> 00:48:43,120
Hong, I managed to unlock
even your stubborn heart before.

452
00:48:43,200 --> 00:48:45,720
This'll be easy.

453
00:48:45,800 --> 00:48:48,640
Just hurry up and open it.
You're making me nervous.

454
00:48:48,720 --> 00:48:50,680
Hey, I was just kidding.

455
00:49:25,040 --> 00:49:28,720
-You okay? Come on.
-Enough.

456
00:49:28,800 --> 00:49:30,320
Hold on.

457
00:49:30,400 --> 00:49:32,240
-Oh, the bag.
-Give me a second.

458
00:49:33,520 --> 00:49:35,080
Can we just leave the kid here?

459
00:49:35,160 --> 00:49:37,000
I told you, I can't carry him.

460
00:49:37,080 --> 00:49:39,440
By the time we drag him to the car,
it'll be dark.

461
00:49:39,520 --> 00:49:42,520
We can't just leave him, bro.
He's one of us.

462
00:49:42,600 --> 00:49:45,320
"One of us"? I don't have
any siblings. I'm an only child.

463
00:49:45,400 --> 00:49:46,680
That's not what I meant.

464
00:49:46,760 --> 00:49:48,760
-Hurry.
-You're the strong one.

465
00:49:48,840 --> 00:49:51,040
Can't you carry him by yourself?

466
00:49:51,120 --> 00:49:52,240
Come on, bro.

467
00:49:52,320 --> 00:49:54,840
At this rate, it'll be morning
before we get him to the car.

468
00:49:54,920 --> 00:49:55,920
Hurry up.

469
00:49:56,000 --> 00:49:57,800
Eat less, man. You're way too heavy.

470
00:50:31,360 --> 00:50:33,960
You fat kid, did you swallow
a bag of rocks or something?

471
00:50:35,200 --> 00:50:36,960
Hurry up. Let's do this.

472
00:50:38,240 --> 00:50:40,440
Alright, one, two, three, lift!

473
00:50:42,240 --> 00:50:45,760
Easy, bro. Watch it.

474
00:51:09,440 --> 00:51:10,880
Damn it.

475
00:51:10,960 --> 00:51:14,600
It's getting dark. Didn't you say this
would be easier than opening my heart?

476
00:52:05,000 --> 00:52:06,320
Done!

477
00:52:10,840 --> 00:52:12,920
Amazing. That was straight out of a movie.

478
00:52:13,000 --> 00:52:16,360
Kid, you can only pull this off
if you're really cool.

479
00:52:19,240 --> 00:52:20,640
Look at this.

480
00:52:20,720 --> 00:52:23,800
Ta-da!

481
00:52:27,160 --> 00:52:29,000
Why is there so little?

482
00:52:29,080 --> 00:52:32,720
Weren't they talking about 800 million?
This doesn't even look like ten million.

483
00:52:35,800 --> 00:52:38,240
Did Wisut see through us already?

484
00:52:43,960 --> 00:52:48,160
I told you it'd be dark
by the time we got him to the car.

485
00:52:49,680 --> 00:52:50,920
And now it is.

486
00:52:57,880 --> 00:52:59,680
-Chen, hide.
-Huh?

487
00:52:59,760 --> 00:53:01,760
Bro, what? What is it?

488
00:53:03,600 --> 00:53:04,880
What is it?

489
00:53:05,600 --> 00:53:07,600
-Come here.
-What?

490
00:53:22,640 --> 00:53:26,720
Weren't you supposed to call the police
after we moved all the money out?

491
00:53:26,800 --> 00:53:28,320
Exactly.

492
00:53:28,400 --> 00:53:29,600
<i>Koh!</i>

493
00:53:29,680 --> 00:53:33,000
<i>The police are all over</i>
<i>the front of the house!</i>

494
00:53:33,080 --> 00:53:34,440
Huh? What did you say?

495
00:53:43,680 --> 00:53:46,680
How did the police get here?
Everything's falling apart.

496
00:53:47,560 --> 00:53:49,840
-Sergeant, open the gate.
-Yes, sir.

497
00:53:49,920 --> 00:53:51,960
The rest of you,
wait for my signal to move in.

498
00:53:59,200 --> 00:54:01,680
Everyone, we've been set up.
We need to get out of here now.

499
00:54:02,600 --> 00:54:04,760
How are we supposed to escape
with cops all over the place?

500
00:54:13,160 --> 00:54:14,200
Bro.

501
00:54:14,280 --> 00:54:15,360
Where did you park the car?

502
00:54:15,440 --> 00:54:16,840
One street over. Why?

503
00:54:18,000 --> 00:54:20,200
Chen, tell Phayak

504
00:54:20,280 --> 00:54:22,320
to bring the car around to the back.

505
00:54:22,400 --> 00:54:25,040
I remember from the blueprints,
there's a small back exit.

506
00:54:25,120 --> 00:54:27,080
Okay, got it.

507
00:54:30,240 --> 00:54:31,760
Roger.

508
00:54:31,840 --> 00:54:33,960
Bro!

509
00:54:34,480 --> 00:54:37,480
Chen, find a way to distract the police.

510
00:54:37,560 --> 00:54:39,080
Draw as many of them away as you can.

511
00:54:39,160 --> 00:54:42,640
Hang on, Koh. Tell me first.
How am I supposed to distract the police?

512
00:54:42,720 --> 00:54:46,040
Any way you can.
I don't care how. Just do it.

513
00:54:47,920 --> 00:54:49,200
Hey, what?

514
00:54:50,000 --> 00:54:50,840
Go.

515
00:54:50,920 --> 00:54:53,120
Go where? Let's move.

516
00:54:59,560 --> 00:55:01,640
Quick, hide.

517
00:55:06,720 --> 00:55:08,080
What are you doing, Chen?

518
00:55:21,200 --> 00:55:22,560
Officer!

519
00:55:25,400 --> 00:55:26,240
Take cover!

520
00:55:30,480 --> 00:55:31,680
After him!

521
00:55:36,120 --> 00:55:38,040
-Go! Move!
-Go!

522
00:55:38,120 --> 00:55:39,240
-Hurry up, Risa!
-Move!

523
00:55:41,840 --> 00:55:43,080
Wait.

524
00:55:45,440 --> 00:55:46,600
They're inside the house.

525
00:55:49,440 --> 00:55:51,880
I told you.
Mungkorn's been acting really strange.

526
00:55:51,960 --> 00:55:53,160
Yeah.

527
00:55:53,240 --> 00:55:57,120
<i>He disappeared during the mission.</i>
<i>Then, after Admin's plan fell apart,</i>

528
00:55:57,200 --> 00:55:59,520
<i>he suddenly showed up again</i>
<i>and took Risa with him.</i>

529
00:55:59,600 --> 00:56:01,000
Angpao, check this laptop for me.

530
00:56:01,080 --> 00:56:02,000
Mungkorn's laptop?

531
00:56:02,080 --> 00:56:03,440
What? What is it?

532
00:56:03,520 --> 00:56:05,760
<i>I found it on the second floor</i>
<i>of Wisut's house.</i>

533
00:56:05,840 --> 00:56:08,120
This is ridiculous.
Stop making baseless accusations.

534
00:56:08,200 --> 00:56:09,880
Let's just turn it on

535
00:56:09,960 --> 00:56:11,680
<i>and see what's inside.</i>

536
00:56:11,760 --> 00:56:15,200
<i>We'll find out</i>
<i>if he's been hiding anything from us.</i>

537
00:56:15,280 --> 00:56:17,000
-Angpao's calling.
-Ris?

538
00:56:17,080 --> 00:56:18,440
I'm with Mungkorn right now.

539
00:56:18,520 --> 00:56:19,840
Don't trust him yet.

540
00:56:19,920 --> 00:56:21,600
<i>Are you finally</i>
<i>going to tell me everything?</i>

541
00:56:21,680 --> 00:56:23,960
I was planning to tell you
the whole truth anyway.

542
00:56:24,040 --> 00:56:26,520
Then tell me. If you don't answer me now,

543
00:56:26,600 --> 00:56:27,800
we're done.

544
00:56:27,880 --> 00:56:29,120
Yes, I'm Admin.

545
00:57:14,960 --> 00:57:19,760
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
